<title>USA: House panel mulls $270 mln FY98 EEP spending cap.</title>
<headline>House panel mulls $270 mln FY98 EEP spending cap.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of the U.S. House Appropriations subcommittee on agriculture are mulling a $270 million cap on funding for the Export Enhancement Program for fiscal 1998 as part of an overhaul spending bill to fund USDA programs.</p>
<p>The Clinton Administration requested $500 million for EEP, which is used to subsidize wheat and other agriculture exports. However, panel chairman Rep. Joe Skeen, Republican from New Mexico, said his committee needed to take funds from EEP to fully fund crop insurance in fiscal 1998.</p>
<p>A vote on the bill is expected later this morning.</p>
</text>
